**/test-results/*.png
**/playwright-report/**/*.png

# Root AGENTS.md and docs/ROADMAP.md are tracked PRF entrypoints.
# Per-developer notes remain untracked in AGENTS.local.md / CONTEXT.md.
docs/ROADMAP.md
!/docs/ROADMAP.md
docs/adr/
CONTEXT.md

# Production-ready action plan package (Post-PRF stabilization program,
# baseline `2991e5e2`). Tracked because it is the active roadmap
# addendum governing CR-* and ST-* work units. See ROADMAP-ADDENDUM.md.
# `!/docs/roadmap/` is required: without it, `docs/roadmap` stays excluded, git
# never descends into it, and the negations below match nothing. It is re-closed
# right after with `docs/roadmap/*`, so the exemption covers the addendum package
# and not the whole directory, which would otherwise pull in ephemeral files such
# as docs/roadmap/INSTALL.md.
!/docs/roadmap/
docs/roadmap/*
!/docs/roadmap/production-ready/
!/docs/roadmap/production-ready/**/

# NOTE: docs/debts/ is deliberately NOT exempted. It looks like it should be —
# `advisory_ignore_backing_contract` reads DEBT-SEC-001 in CI, so the register
# has to be tracked. But exempting the directory also exposes DEBT-SDDK-002..005,
# which exist on disk and were never committed, and DEBT-SDDK-004/005/006 all
# carry the line "local only, NEVER pushed to remote (ephemeral per
# AGENTS.md)". Making them trackable by default is a policy decision about the
# local-only rule of 2026-06-24, not a side effect of fixing the negations.
# DEBT-SEC-001 is tracked because a gate depends on it, and that exception is
# recorded rather than smuggled in. Tracked separately.

# C8 recertification openspec change (Post-PRF stabilization).
!/openspec/changes/2026-09-26-c8-recertification/
!/openspec/changes/2026-09-26-c8-recertification/**/
!/openspec/changes/2026-09-26-architecture-boundary-hardening/
!/openspec/changes/2026-09-26-architecture-boundary-hardening/**/

