# `crates/cognicode-cli/src/bin/` holds SOURCE, not build output: the package
# produces several binaries (`cogh`, `cognicode`, `cognicode-release`).
# A very common global ignore pattern is a bare `bin/`, which silently drops NEW
# files added there while leaving already-tracked ones alone. That is exactly how
# `src/bin/release.rs` was lost on the first v0.95.0 release attempt: local builds
# passed and CI failed with "can't find bin". A repository-level negation wins
# over core.excludesFile, so declare the layout here.
!crates/cognicode-cli/src/bin/
# Same protection for cognicode-explorer/src/bin/ (E2.W2 introduced
# `cognicode-control-plane` there on 2026-09-25). The bin itself was
# designed and tested locally, but committed without the source file
# because this blanket ignore was not negated for explorer. Bug
# detected on first pr-ci.yml run after E2.W2 (workflow could not
# find the bin source file). Mirror the cli exemption.
!crates/cognicode-explorer/src/bin/
sandbox/scripts/tests/__pycache__/
*.cdx.json
*.cdx.xml

# Compat matrix binaries (Post-PRF L1.3): binarios legacy para tests
# de compat (extraídos de releases publicados, no commiteados).
sandbox/.compat/

# Python bytecode caches. scripts/ci/test_select_suites.py is now run by the
# PR-CI `check` job, so running the suite locally produces these. Without the
# ignore they show up as untracked noise on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# SDDK orchestration scratch. `sddk` writes these into the working directory
# when a command is run from the repo root; they are session output, never
# project state. The unit's real evidence lives under docs/, not here.
.sddk-scratch/
out-*.json
